//! `lower(Grammar) -> LoweredGrammar` — translate the surface IR
//! to GIR for parser code generation.
//!
//! This is the planning phase of the pipeline:
//!
//! ```text
//! .g4 source ──parse──► Grammar (surface IR, ir.wado)
//!                ──lower──► LoweredGrammar (gir.wado)
//!                ──emit──► Wado source
//! ```
//!
//! Every codegen-time decision (rule shape, multi-alt dispatch, LR
//! precedence, per-call-site FOLLOW args, group shape, repeat strategy,
//! field deduplication, scan/parse symmetry) is committed here so the emit
//! layer can translate structurally without consulting the surface IR.
//!
//! ## What lower handles
//!
//! `lower` covers every surface-IR shape — single- and multi-alt rules,
//! left-recursive rules (atom + lr_alts), every Group classifier
//! (`Transparent`, `SingleAlt`, `TokenOnly`, `SimpleCst`, `General`),
//! every Repeat kind (`Star` / `Plus` / `Optional`, greedy and
//! non-greedy), `Not` complements, and scalar / list (`+=`) Labels.
//! Multi-alt dispatch is `Direct` for disjoint first-sets or `Tournament`
//! for overlapping fully-scannable alts.
//!
//! The tail-position caller-FOLLOW repair is threaded at runtime (a
//! `FollowArg` per `RuleRef` call site, a `gate_caller_follow` flag per
//! tail Repeat), so greedy Repeats stay `Plain` and yield via
//! `follow_yields` at run time. Repeats over General-Group inners share
//! the per-rule `group_counter` between the outer field name and the
//! inner variant.
//!
//! `codegen::generate` calls `lower` and feeds the result through the emit
//! layer (`parser_gen.wado` / `codegen.wado`).

use {
